# Vendored third-party emulator trees.
#
# romwbw_emu/ is 79 MB of the 84 MB in this directory - a RomWBW emulator
# checkout that is not this project's code. Tracking it would dominate the
# repository without contributing any history for anything written here. It
# stays on disk; build_rom.sh's ../../Tools/bin/tasm references are likewise
# relative to a checkout layout this tree does not have.

romwbw_emu/
zeta/
romwbw_emu.bak/

# Build products. The emulator is plain C with no separate build directory, so
# the objects land next to their sources.  The per-device object files are
# covered by *.o above.
#
# zeta_sbc_v2/ used to be listed here as though it were a binary.  It is a
# source directory, and listing it silently untracked the whole Zeta SBC V2
# model: the model 47e6b9e wired into the build, and that every DS1302 fix
# since has landed in.  A model the build compiles and the repository does not
# have is a model the next checkout does not build - and it is worse than that,
# because a fix to it sits uncommitted and nothing reports it.  The
# calendar-carry fix in 6ae6a3a was exactly that, and had to be caught by hand.
#
# What the build actually compiles from that directory is ONE file.  Measured
# two ways, both agreeing: `make -C emulator info` prints the resolved SRCS
# list, and building this emulator from a copy of `git ls-files` alone compiles
# and links zeta_sbc_v2/emu_ds1302.c and nothing else from here.  The other 23
# .c files are the rest of the model - a real Zeta SBC V2, with its own FDC,
# PPI, CTC and CP/M layers - and none of it is in this build.  47e6b9e left
# them out on purpose: they may carry symbols that collide with z80pack.c, and
# pulling them in would risk a working emulator for no gain.
#
# So they stay ignored, which is a decision about what to *compile*, not a claim
# that they are build products.  They remain on disk.  The one that is compiled
# is un-ignored here rather than force-added, so it is a normal tracked file:
# see tools/check_emulator_sources.rb, which fails the build if a source the
# Makefile compiles is untracked or still matched by a rule.  Adding a file to
# SRCS means un-excluding it here too, and that gate is what will say so.
zeta_sbc_v2/*
!zeta_sbc_v2/emu_ds1302.c
!zeta_sbc_v2/emulator.h
*.o
*.bak
z80pack-emu
romwbw_emu
decode_boot
mem_offset_test
mem_verify_test
test_memory
test_memory_dump
test_debug
trace_boot
trace_ldir
test_ldir_complete
test_ldir_debug
test_ldir_fixed
test_ldir_simple
test_ldir_trace
test_ldir_verify

# Assembled test binaries and images.
*.bin
*.rom
*.img

# Captured output from test runs. These are regenerated on every run and were
# the bulk of the noise in the working tree.
*.log
*.txt
capture.txt
console.txt
out.log
out.txt
verbose.txt
trace.log
trace2.log
boot_output.txt
test_output.txt
